From 55db34d9ca6ffd35c95be339a2f139d2454f16cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kenichi Ishibashi <bashi@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:29:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [M159] Scope AcceptCHFrameObserver lifetime to the active
 loader leg

Original change's description:
> Scope AcceptCHFrameObserver lifetime to the active loader leg
>
> Previously, NavigationURLLoaderImpl bound a single AcceptCHFrameObserver
> in its constructor and kept the ReceiverSet open for the entire
> navigation. When an interceptor such as Service Worker navigation
> preload copied ResourceRequest, the cloned observer pipe outlived
> redirects, loader resets, and response unbinding. A late
> OnAcceptCHFrameReceived() call on that stale pipe could then restart the
> loader after OnReceiveResponse() had already unbound endpoints and
> started asynchronous header parsing.
>
> Tie the observer receivers to the loader that is currently active.
> A fresh observer is bound when an HTTP(S) loader is started, and all
> observer pipes are closed when that loader stops being the active,
> not-yet-responded leg (reset, handoff to an interceptor, response,
> or a redirect that switches loaders). Clone() and
> OnAcceptCHFrameReceived() are ignored outside that window, and a
> restart is only accepted for the navigation's own origin.
>
> On the network side, AcceptCHFrameInterceptor treats a closed observer
> pipe as "no restart", so a request whose observer was closed proceeds
> with net::OK instead of hanging. The .mojom comments now document this
> lifetime contract.
>
> NO_IFTTT=Moved OnAcceptCHFrameReceivedReturnLocation from .cc to .h.
>
